# Pinned versions of every external dependency. restore.sh reads this.

# --- LLVM ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must be the revision triton@$TRITON_SHA pins: triton-shared-opt prints MLIR as
# text and the python bindings parse it, and the assembly format is not stable
# across major releases. `run.py doctor` reports MISMATCH if they drift.
# Our fork at ac5dc54d -- the revision triton pins -- plus the VCIX ops with no
# destination, which stage 5 mints and upstream MLIR does not model, and an init
# tensor keeping its encoding in ElementwiseToLinalg.
# THAT REPOSITORY BUILDS IT. This one downloads the asset tagged llvm23-<sha12>
# and never compiles LLVM -- see setup/restore.sh's llvm step.
LLVM_REPO=https://github.com/PSAL-POSTECH/llvm-project.git
LLVM_BRANCH=torchsim-llvm23
LLVM_SHA=f9dd1012675ff3fa12954375ed5a2e67059e6c43
# --- triton -------------------------------------------------------------------
# A main-branch commit, not the v3.6.0 tag: the tag still pins LLVM 22.
TRITON_REPO=https://github.com/triton-lang/triton.git
TRITON_SHA=df38505e451a1541555379bcf378be9e8c00545c
# Patches in setup/patches/triton/. nvvm_reduction_kind_compatibility is
# required (NVVM ReductionKind API moved in this LLVM); libdevice_sigmoid is not.

# --- triton_shared ------------------------------------------------------------
# OUR FORK, and the patch list is gone: every fix is a COMMIT there now.
TRITON_SHARED_REPO=git@github.com:PSAL-POSTECH/triton_shared.git
TRITON_SHARED_BRANCH=torchsim
# THE BINARY EVERY MEASUREMENT HERE WAS MADE WITH, which the old pin did not
# describe: it stopped at 725c6c0 while TORCHSIM_COMPILE_TRITON_SHARED_OPT pointed at a build
# of refactor/v0.8. The merge is a fast-forward of that branch, so this commit's
# tree IS what was measured -- the pin caught up, nothing moved under it.
#
#     1c8d64b  Merge refactor/v0.8
#       298b8f9  Merge refactor/v0.9: PtrAnalysis reports its demotions
#         771878d  ... and stops calling a data-dependent address one
#           7d6b8dd  ... nor one with two bases
#             16d9440  tts.load/store verify their mask box
#               ee33e11  a nested loop carries a mask bound too
#                 78e0d17  the classic and memref routes deleted
#                   6f99cf0  the axis split, the step slot, and the missing
#                            park in visitOperandAddptr
#                     ...    the PtrAnalysis refactor, seventeen commits
#                       91ceb26  Four identities move down from torchsim-compile's c01
#                         00613e1  A clamp is not affine, so not a stride
#                           a1fa0d9  The loop carries the scalar too
#                             f7b34b5  A bound this cannot read as a constant
#                                      may still have a floor   <- the pin
#
# THIS ONE IS A MUST, AND THE TREE ABOVE IT ALREADY DEPENDED ON IT. develop
# shipped the torchsim-compile half of three of these and left the pin behind, so the tree
# was red against the toolchain it declared: 12 kernels, 9 of them dying in
# stage 3 on an expect_ir that names the arm triton-shared no longer takes.
# Measured both ways on one binary swap -- 12 red at 6f99cf0, 12 green at
# f7b34b5 -- which is what makes this a pin defect and not a code defect.
#
# THE PAIRS, so a future bisect does not have to find them: torchsim-compile's
# `Five identities leave c01 for triton-shared` needs 91ceb26, its
# `The axes a mask narrows are not "clamped"` needs 00613e1, and
# `Two silent miscompiles stop being expected` needs a1fa0d9. A torchsim-compile commit
# whose triton-shared half is past the pin is not shippable on its own.
#
# THE PARK BELOW IT IS THE ONE THAT CHANGED ANSWERS. visitOperandAddptr was the
# only merge point that did not call parkWrapOnTheGatheredAxis, so `x % W` added
# to an already-gathered pointer lost its modulo and the address came out one
# term short -- silently, with a plausible number.
#
# A MUST FOR A SOURCE BUILD. p01 reads `!ptr.ptr`, a REGISTERED type, instead of
# parsing `!tt.ptr<f32>` out of a spelling tt is unregistered for; the pass that
# leaves that type is --triton-to-ptr and it is in stage 3's pipeline now.
#
# THE ONE ABOVE IT IS A SHOULD, NOT A MUST: --triton-to-structured gains an
# off-by-default `report-demotions` and nothing else, and 437/437 came out
# byte-identical with it in. It is pinned anyway because the binary here was
# built from it, and a pin that does not describe the binary is the failure
# this variable exists to prevent -- which it had just been caught doing.
#
#     1d791be  One decline, one report: the pass says why it keeps its
#              tt.load                                      <- the pin
#     9cbd041  The cut says why it refuses a stepped axis, and the retry
#              un-mints both of `x // K`'s slots
#     344b413  A cast carries a value by its direction, not by its name
#     109a6da  A split does not cross an scf boundary, so the flag can be
#              on by default
#     e1cd4dc  A split axis crossing a loop refuses instead of aborting
#     30e0344  A remainder bound at or above the modulus excludes nothing
#     7c71a5a  The base offset survives being an iter-arg twice
#     bc023e6  A constant that arrived as a Value is still a constant
#     916b872  One modulo per address, and the refusal says so
#     e8c1f4d  The wall a gather has one axis gets its name
#     4aef176  The sum wrap gets a test, now that it can be spelled
#     6d1d6b9  make_tptr could not read back what it printed
#
# ALSO A SHOULD. tts.make_tptr's two tail slots gain a custom parser so a
# flat_shape without a base_offset reads back; the PRINTED form does not move
# and 459/459 stage 3 outputs are byte-identical, so nothing here needs it. It
# is pinned because this tree measured against it. The one above it is TEST
# ONLY -- the sum wrap finally gets a lit file -- so the binary does not move
# between the two, and the sweep above was measured at either.
#
# AND THE HEAD OF THE LIST IS A REPORTING FIX, not a behaviour one:
# TritonToUnstructured had six declines that said the same thing three ways --
# three `emitError` that exit 0, and two that said nothing. Eight of this
# corpus's modules take one of those declines and all eight now name the op and
# the reason. No IR moves.
#
# AND THE PIN BELOW IT IS A SHOULD TOO. Two address walks read arith.index_cast
# as value-preserving, which it is only when it widens; the narrowing spelling
# let a bit mask fold to a wrap that names a different address. Then a stepped
# axis meeting a split fell TWO rungs where the same flag turned OFF reaches an
# index table -- the cut's refusal was anonymous, so the un-minting retry never
# ran. Nothing in this corpus writes either shape: rung1 2006, rung2 176, rung3
# 126 at both pins, and 1347 artifacts are byte-identical. This tree moves for
# the soundness and for the rung it stops losing, not for an output today.
# AND ANOTHER MUST, FOUND THE SAME WAY -- the tree ahead of its pin. torchsim-compile
# 422f3f8 reads tts.load's FIFTH operand segment (the elementwise mask that
# 62eab23 added when a mask's low end became a value), and dd76247 deleted c01
# because e936f14 merged the rest of it upstream. At 1d791be every kernel dies
# in p03 on `IndexError: list index out of range` -- smoke/add included; at
# e936f14 all six smoke kernels reach 04-adapted.mlir. A fresh restore at the
# old pin could not compile ANYTHING this tree ships.
#
#     e936f14  Merge the rest of torchsim-compile's c01, which stopped one round short
#       62eab23  A mask's lower bound may be a VALUE, so the box's low end
#                gets a dynamic half                       <- the pin
#     0f006ac  ExternElementwise: __nv_powif and __nv_powi are math.fpowi  <- the pin
#              p00 (e79c9bb) keeps no alias for powi: at e936f14 it stays an extern
#              call and p00 refuses it (ops_math_pow_int_exponent).
#     0cf7416  adapt-ttgir: TritonGPU encodings carried through the tensor IR
#              The layouts are decided in TritonGPU IR (adapt-ttgir), and a kernel's
#              encodings die in triton_shared at an older pin.
#     b05962d  a converted gathered pointer keeps its gather pointer
#     40ee634  MatmulConverter: tt.dot's C is linalg.matmul's outs
#     6a5ee0f  triton-to-ptr keeps a pointer tile's encoding
#     5454c93  CumSumConverter carries a scan's discardable attributes
#     7b79204  PtrAnalysis: knownPtrs keeps the analysis state
#     48afb14  revert of the born-wide mask (9310b07) and keep-reduce-axis (3b4e93d),
#              both written for the first materializer          <- the pin
TRITON_SHARED_SHA=48afb1488a6778762d43d009094b52cf430a68f9

# --- spike --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The fork with no accelerator of its own -- $VCIX_MODEL answers instead, and
# riscv/vcix_accel_extension.cc is the marker. The pin is the submodule's, not
# a copy here; toolchain_tag.sh hashes the gitlink, so the tag still moves.
_VCIX_SETUP="$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../third_party/vcix-accelerator/setup"
[ -f "$_VCIX_SETUP/versions.env" ] \
  || { echo "third_party/vcix-accelerator is empty -- git submodule update --init" >&2; return 1 2>/dev/null || exit 1; }
eval "$(cd "$_VCIX_SETUP/.." && . setup/versions.env >/dev/null 2>&1 \
        && declare -p SPIKE_REPO SPIKE_SHA GEM5_URL GEM5_SHA256 GEM5_TARGET \
                      TOOLCHAIN_URL TOOLCHAIN_SHA256 PK_REPO PK_SHA)"
# A MUST FOR THIS COMPILER, not a should, and for two reasons now.
#
# A wrapped access is lowered as several strided transfers sharing one tile, and
# each names its rows with the descriptor's box plus a per-axis "skip" bit in
# flags. An older spike does not read that bit, so every piece FILLS the rows its
# siblings just wrote and the tile keeps only the last one.
#
# AND THE DESCRIPTOR IS 160 BYTES NOW. +144/+152 carry the argument's range, and
# a masked-off write is parked OUTSIDE it on purpose -- nothing is reserved
# behind an output any more. An older spike does not read those fields, so that
# write lands for real, in memory the wrapper no longer allocates.
#
# AND AN INDIRECT INDEX IS SIGNED. The DMA loads it with load_uint8/16/32/64
# and the first three ZERO EXTEND a value the program means as signed: -128 in a
# four-byte field reads as 4294967168 and the address lands 2^34 past the tile.
# Eight bytes was always right, which is why this compiler used to widen every
# index tile to i64 -- a buffer and a copy per transfer. `df08f17` reads it
# signed and that widening is gone. The branch below is named after it; the
# reason went unrecorded here for a round because nothing in the suite held a
# negative index. ptr_gather_negative_index.py does now, in i32.
#
# All three are wrong NUMBERS, not errors. `vlane_start` (+133), pinned at
# 8e46ad6, is gone -- a piece names its rows with the box instead.
# AND THE CROSS-LANE UNIT, WHICH IS A MUST BY THE OLDEST REASON AGAIN. Stage 5
# mints `vcix.iv` with the unit's SIMM5 (torchsim-compile 479926b / 0de0301) and b0d82d0
# has no cross_lane_unit.cc: smoke/reduce dies on Spike with `An illegal
# instruction was executed!` at inst 0x2e82305b (custom-2). The unit landed
# 58bb96f (merge, 09-14), its three-field SIMM5 9e8f57c pairs with torchsim-compile
# 479926b, and the pattern-beside-the-data 9afe8a0 pairs with torchsim-compile 0de0301.
#
#     9f555b4  The install is a build product, not a thing we ship  <- the pin
#       9afe8a0  xlu: the pattern arrives beside the data
#         9e8f57c  The five bits are three fields, and an all-gather is one pass
#           58bb96f  Merge the cross-lane unit

# --- the distribution layer (setup/system.sh) ---------------------------------
# THE BASE IMAGE IS ubuntu:22.04 AND CARRIES NONE OF THIS. It used to be
# ghcr.io/psal-postech/torchsim_tnpu, which shipped its own LLVM, gem5, spike and TOGSim
# beside the ones built here -- 8.53 GB compressed, most of it a second copy. What the base
# really gave that nothing here rebuilds was python3.11, the TOGSim pair below, and the
# RISC-V toolchain + pk now restored by the `riscv` step.
#
# cmake 3.26.4 and conan 1.56.0 are the versions TOGSim's conanfile.txt was resolved with;
# restore.sh's build_tools() keeps LLVM 23's cmake 3.31.6 in a venv so these stay put.
HOST_CMAKE_VERSION=3.26.4
CONAN_VERSION=1.56.0
# The reference values every kernel is scored against: tests/runtime/stages.py calls
# spec.make_inputs(torch). CPU wheels only -- nothing here has, or wants, a GPU.
TORCH_VERSION=2.10.0

# --- install locations (pytorchsim_triton_compiler/config.py defaults) -------------------------------
# The triton and triton_shared checkouts are SIBLINGS under /workspace, like
# every other dependency. They used to live inside a /workspace/hexagon-mlir
# clone -- HEXAGON_MLIR_ROOT -- which read as a dependency and was not one:
# qualcomm's tree was never cloned by these scripts and nothing under it was
# ever read except those two subdirectories, both of which are somebody else's
# repo anyway (triton-lang upstream, and our own fork). The variables recording
# its provenance were declared and never referenced by any script; the pin's
# actual origin is a comment where the pin is, which is where it belongs.
LLVM_ROOT=/workspace/LLVM_DIR/llvm-project
LLVM_INSTALL=/workspace/LLVM_DIR/llvm-project/build/install
# NOT /workspace/triton: that shadows the `triton` package as a namespace
# package for anything run from /workspace, and `import triton` then finds a
# directory with no __version__.
TRITON_ROOT=/workspace/triton-src
TRITON_SHARED_ROOT=/workspace/triton_shared
SPIKE_ROOT=/workspace/riscv-isa-sim
GEM5_ROOT=/workspace/gem5
# Where the base image put them, so TORCHSIM_COMPILE_PK and RISCV do not move.
RISCV_ROOT=/workspace/riscv
PK_ROOT=/workspace/riscv-pk
PK_BIN=/workspace/riscv-pk/build/pk
# The model Spike loads with --extlib; its source is the submodule.
VCIX_BUILD=/workspace/vcix-build
VCIX_MODEL=/workspace/vcix-build/libtpu.so
TRITON_VENV=/workspace/mlir-env

